{
  "$comment": [
    "The GATE set: 15 scenarios that measure, and never teach.",
    "",
    "Disjoint from `optimizer-truth.json` from day one, in three ways at once: no scenario id,",
    "no turn text and no order id appears in both files (`tests/scenarios.test.ts` asserts all",
    "three). Disjointness is the cheapest defence there is against the loop overfitting its own",
    "gate — evals-research-synthesis-2026-08.md §7 ranks a sealed dev/gate split first by",
    "evidence strength, and §6.5 is where the two-budget shape comes from: a small optimizer",
    "set (20 items; Decagon's ablation found 20 samples peak and 500 actively worse) and a",
    "gate set that grows toward the ~150-450 items real statistical power needs.",
    "",
    "Fifteen is NOT that number, and the driver says so out loud: `--gate` prints the set's",
    "minimum detectable effect alongside the score, so nobody reads a 15-item result as a",
    "shipping receipt. It is a starting gate whose job is to catch gross regressions and to",
    "make the harness for a bigger one real.",
    "",
    "`reaction` is null on every scenario here and the driver posts no outcomes and no",
    "telemetry in `--gate` mode. That is the mechanism, not the intention: a gate episode that",
    "reached littleDB would become run history the dream reads, and the next dream would be",
    "tuned on the very items meant to judge it.",
    "",
    "Shape and grading semantics: see the header of `optimizer-truth.json`."
  ],
  "set": "gate",
